      "category": "Lecture de tableau",
      "question": "What are the main ethnic groups of Madagascar?",
      "in_scope": true,
      "answer": "The main ethnic groups of Madagascar include the Merina, who form the largest Malagasy ethnic subgroup at approximately 26% of the population, and the Betsimisaraka, Tsimihety, and Sakalava, who are among the largest coastal ethnic subgroups. Additionally, there are Chinese, Indian, and Comoran minorities, as well as a small European (primarily French) populace. The Malagasy ethnic group as a whole forms over 90% of Madagascar's population and is typically divided into 18 ethnic subgroups. \n\nSource: [Ethnic groups] | Chunk #112, #113, #115",
