      "question": "How did political power change in Madagascar between 2009 and 2014?",
      "in_scope": true,
      "answer": "In early 2009, opposition leader and then-mayor of Antananarivo, Andry Rajoelina, led a movement that resulted in the unconstitutional removal of President Marc Ravalomanana from power, an event widely condemned as a coup d'état. In March 2009, Rajoelina was declared by the Supreme Court as president of the High Transitional Authority, an interim governing body responsible for moving the country toward presidential elections. In 2010, a new constitution was adopted by referendum, establishing a Fourth Republic. Constitutional governance was restored in January 2014. \n\nSource: [Independent state] | Chunk #50",
